<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Hardened runtime, no exceptions — least privilege for a vault app.

    Verrou deliberately requests NO entitlement exceptions:
      * It runs no in-process JIT. WKWebView executes JavaScript in Apple's
        separately-signed `com.apple.WebKit.WebContent` process, so the host
        app needs neither `allow-jit` nor `allow-unsigned-executable-memory`.
      * mlock/Zeroize, Touch ID (LocalAuthentication), and per-app keychain
        access all work for Developer ID (non-sandboxed) apps without an
        entitlement.

    If a future dependency genuinely needs one, add the single specific key
    here and document why — never broaden blindly.

    NOTE: this app is NOT sandboxed (com.apple.security.app-sandbox absent),
    which is correct for Developer-ID-signed direct distribution.
  -->
</dict>
</plist>
